cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Antumbra: making supervision measurable"
message: "If you use this dataset or method, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Blomqvist
    given-names: Martin
    email: cm.blomqvist@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/MartinBlomqvistDev/antumbra"
abstract: >-
  Sweden publishes the conditions it imposes on large livestock installations
  but discloses the outcome of its own inspections in redacted form, to varying
  degrees between county administrative boards. The responsible agency reports a
  51 percentage point spread between counties in the share of inspections
  finding deficiencies, and states that the difference cannot be read out of the
  statistics. Antumbra measures that gap using the authorities' own records, and
  compares it against the European Commission's audits of member state control
  systems.
keywords:
  - public administration
  - transparency
  - freedom of information
  - official controls
  - animal welfare
  - open data
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
